  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1045 PM CDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\nThis shortwave and its resultant precip will fizzle out on Sunday \nevening. After this, the surface pattern looks fairly nondescript on \nMonday and Tuesday for Middle TN, resulting in benign weather and \nmild temperatures. This is a brief transitional period between \nweather systems. Forecast surface analyses place a strong low \npressure system over the Central Plains on Tuesday afternoon, which \nis expected to deepen to the point of occlusion by the time it \nreaches Middle TN on Wednesday. While details are still fuzzy this \nfar out, models are in fairly good agreement on another shot of rain \nassociated with a cold front passing through the TN Valley on \nWednesday. The more favorable overlap of instability and shear is \ndisplaced to the south over central MS/AL, but we'll still most \nlikely have enough instability to support thunderstorms during the \nFROPA on Wednesday afternoon.  \n\nAs the surface low continues to deepen after migrating off to the \nVirginias on Thursday and Friday, wraparound showers from this same \nsystem will continue to impact parts of Middle TN for several days. \nBroad upper level troughing per the LREF supports much cooler \ntemperatures (finally near normal in the mid 60s) and 20-40% PoPs \nthrough at least Friday morning. We finally dry back out on Friday \nevening but remain cool.",
